  "query_preview": "..\nAs of 121 PM Thursday... \n\nKEY MESSAGE 1... Dry weather forecast through the middle of next \nweek with near normal temperatures. \n\nHigh pressure remains in place across western PA this afternoon, \nwith ridging extending southward through the Mid Atlantic. Meanwhile \nSubtropical Storm Josephine remains off the coast of New England and \ncontinues to rapidly accelerate away from the CONUS as it treks \nnortheastward. Looking aloft, a dry mid level shortwave trough is \ndiving southward through central PA into MD, while broad longwave \nridging remains in place across the entirety of the eastern US. \n\nThe dry shortwave will move through late tonight into Friday, with \nlittle impact to our daily weather other than to increase cloud \ncover as winds take on a more northeasterly component through the \nday. Post-frontal stratocu is forecast across the Coastal Plain and \nNortheast Piedmont on Friday in the wake of the front as winds take \non a more northeasterly component, although there should still be \nmore clouds than sun. Temps should be a few degrees cooler Friday \nafternoon vs. today.\n\nAfter that, weak high pressure should build in again from the north, \nallowing temperatures to moderate a bit but still remain within a \ncategory of normal for late October. Another dry shortwave trough \ncould swing through the area by the middle of next week but precip \nchances look remote at best and we'll stick with a dry forecast for \nthe entirety of the next 7 days.",
